record.body:
Created a simple database system to accommodate DominoTiles prefabs in just one place;
Refactored DominoManager.cs to receive references to prefabs from the newly created DominoTilePrefabDatabase;
Moved old tile prefabs to DominoTiles/Old folder;
Rebuilded prefabs as variants;
Changed the DominoHand component to load the tiles from the database;
Changed scenes to use new tile prefabs;

Created a utility class to receive information about the player's current connection status;
Added the internet connection error UI;
Changed the quest rewards buttons to check if the player has an internet connection;

- fixed some warnings that may or may not affect the build running on mobile, in the "dive" effect animation script;
- fixed a logic in FakeShadowController when a piece is removed from the river minigame;
- added a small deviation during the creation of pieces in the river minigame, to add random pieces
- added a shuffle to the position of spawned domino pieces to increase the difficulty a bit

Added support for instantiating UI screen using the GameUIManager.
It can be use in the same way popups are created.
For example.
App.Instance.GameUI.OpenScreen(testScreen, new TestScreenData
{
     RequiredData = 0
});

Added chapter index to flatbuffer puzzle pack. I had a mess trying to get that index, now it is clear the index for a given pack. No need to be careful with the order.
Pack manager now uses a dictionary to avoid dups.

Unlock all levels was not calling:
        DominoPlayerPrefs.SetNumLevelsCompletedForChapter(chapterIndex, chapter.PuzzlesLength); 
        PlayerPrefs.Save();
        
I am not sure how it used to work, but from my tests it is required.

Due to the amount of conflicts that might come up (and the ones that I already solved), it might be a good idea to merge it sooner than later, since there were modifications on the puzzle editor, DominoGameManager.cs, etc.
The existence of this chest won't break the game.

- missing using correct item prefabs or vfx (AFAIK we don't have the visual assets yet)
- still not updating PlayerProfile

Currently the chest is being spawned at every level for testing
```
private void InstantiateChest()
{
	if (!_dominoPuzzle.Puzzle.HasDominoChest && false) return;  //TODO: remove && false
	Instantiate(_dominoChestPrefab).Setup(_chestSpawnPoints);
}
```
